// The check accepted and the build refused "cannot resolve Collection::fold:
// [Array<i64>, Array<Array<i64>>] is not a type constructor" (soak nov25b).
// The check holds each member of the receiver to the one constructor, as it
// holds a union of arrays below an array of their elements' union; the build
// read the union as no application. It is the constructor applied to what
// its members hold.
// Expected trace (both engines): 1.
{ let csize = 'c: Collection |c: 'c| Collection::fold({ let y: [Array<i64>, Array<Array<i64>>] = [1]; y }, 0, |acc, x| acc + 1); csize(["a", [1]]) }
